It is my lunch break, so I grab my backpack.
I walk to a nearby supermarket.
Jonas, Nele, and I are having a barbecue evening in the park today.
I walk through the supermarket and look for our snacks.
I find the potato chips very quickly.
Then I also buy the Brötchen.
We are three people, so I take six Brötchen.
I go to the till and wait.
Finally it is my turn.
"That comes to four Euro eighty, please," says the cashier.
I pay and pack the things into the backpack.
"Do you need the receipt?" he asks me.
"Yes, please," I say.
He gives me the receipt and I leave the supermarket.
The air outside is very warm.
I walk back to the office and am a little annoyed.
The queue at the till was incredibly long.
I had no patience left, because the person in front of me paid entirely with coins.
But now I am simply looking forward to the end of the workday.
